  "preamble": "Fortition and devoicing of the labial glide [w] to the voiceless bilabial stop [p]. Toda changed Proto-Dravidian initial *w to p (*wāy 'mouth' > po·y, *wēr 'root' > pö·r), while neighbouring Kota keeps v (vāy) and Kannada, Tulu and the North Dravidian languages have b instead.",
